# Skills are prose written for agents to read, not source this repository's formatter should reflow. `.agents/skills/`
# and `.claude/skills/` hold symbolic links — into `skills/`, written by scripts/sync-skills.mjs here, and into
# `.agents/skills/` in an application, written by `nocobase skills sync` — so formatting through one would check the
# same file twice under two paths and write the result back into the committed source.
#
# The `**/` matters: an unanchored path matches only the repository root, and each template under packages/templates/
# has both directories of its own. `.gitignore` lists them too, but `--ignore-path` replaces `.gitignore` rather than
# adding to it, and both `pnpm format` and `pnpm format:all` pass it.
#
# The root `skills/` holds this repository's committed Skills, including those users install globally with
# `npx skills add`, and is prose for the same reason.
**/.agents/skills/
**/.claude/skills/
/skills/

# The shadcn/ui skill that the application development Skill embeds is upstream's files, copied unchanged from one shadcn
# release so that a shadcn upgrade replaces the directory wholesale and `diff` against the new release shows everything
# that changed. Formatting them would rewrite most of them and turn that diff into noise. packages/app/app-skills/
# .prettierignore lists the same path for `pnpm format:check` run inside that package; both are needed.
packages/app/app-skills/skills/nocobase-app-development/references/frontend/shadcn/

# The generated Collection artifacts an application keeps under `database/<connection>/collections/`: one JSON file
# per Collection plus a `_manifest.json`, written by `pnpm nocobase collections generate` through a stable serializer so that
# `pnpm nocobase collections generate --check` can regenerate them and compare byte for byte. Prettier collapses their short
# arrays and objects onto single lines, which makes that check report the artifacts as out of date when nothing about
# the schema changed. Each template names the same path in its own `.prettierignore`; a pattern containing a slash is
# anchored to the directory of the file it is written in, so reaching them from here needs the `**/`.
**/database/*/collections/

# An application's migrations and seeds under `database/<connection>/`, which each template names in its own
# `.prettierignore` as well: a run records the checksum of their source and never runs one twice, so reformatting a
# merged one changes no schema but warns every installation that already ran it on its next `nocobase db apply`.
**/database/*/migrations/
**/database/*/seeds/

# Changeset files are written by `changeset add` or by hand and consumed by the changesets tool, which owns their
# format: the repository's `singleQuote` would rewrite `"@nocobase/core": minor` into a form changesets never writes.
# While the branch is in prerelease mode, `changeset version` moves each consumed changeset into `.changeset/pre/`
# unchanged, so that directory needs the same exception: `.changeset/*.md` matches only the top level, and a release
# commit renaming a double-quoted changeset into `pre/` otherwise fails the changed-files Prettier check of the next
# pull request whose diff happens to include it.
.changeset/*.md
.changeset/pre/
!.changeset/README.md
